## Why This Is Asked
Probes ability to design robust E2E tests for streaming pipelines, focusing on exactly-once semantics, replay safety, fault injection, and cross-store validation.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end streaming tests across Kafka, storage, and materialized views
- Exactly-once and idempotent writes
- Replay/failure scenarios and broker partition events
- Tenant data isolation and deterministic mocks
- Observability: SLA validation and latency metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo end-to-end test flow for streaming ingestion
async function testStreamingPipeline() {
  const tenantId = uniqueTenant();
  seedTenant(tenantId);
  produceKafkaEvents(tenantId, 10000);
  waitForSink(tenantId);
  replaySubset(tenantId, 1000);
  verifyNoDuplicates(tenantId);
  simulateBrokerFailure();
  validateEventualConsistency(tenantId);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate idempotency across multiple partitions?
- Which metrics and alarms would you configure for failure scenarios?

